{#- Companies Act trading disclosures (Company, LLP and Business (Names and
    Trading Disclosures) Regulations 2015, reg 25): a company's website has
    to show its registered name, where it's registered, its number and its
    registered office. It doesn't have to be in the footer of every page, so
    at Josh's request (2026-09-27) it lives here, on Contact and Privacy,
    both linked from every page. Don't delete it from BOTH places. -#}
<h2 class="company-details__h">Company details</h2>
<p class="company-details">
  {{ tps.site.legalName }}.
  {%- if tps.site.companyNumber %} Registered in {{ tps.site.registeredIn or "England and Wales" }}, company number {{ tps.site.companyNumber }}.{% endif %}
  {%- if tps.site.registeredOffice %} Registered office: {{ tps.site.registeredOffice }}.{% endif %}
  {%- if tps.site.vatNumber %} VAT number {{ tps.site.vatNumber }}.{% endif %}
</p>
